---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const title = 'OmniShelf closed test — how to join';
const description =
  'OmniShelf is in closed testing. Join with a Google account in two steps, install the Android build, and tell us what broke.';

---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="shell shell--wide">
    <section class="page-head">
      <p class="meta">Closed testing</p>
      <h1>How the closed test works</h1>
      <p class="page-head__lead">
        Google Play has not published OmniShelf publicly yet: the app is in closed testing while
        the last details are checked. That means there is no store listing to browse — there is a
        test link, and a list of accounts allowed to use it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Two steps</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <strong>Ask to be added.</strong> Write to
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=OmniShelf%20closed%20test`}>{SITE.email}</a> from the
          Google account on your phone. Any message will do; the address is the important part.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Open the test link.</strong> Once the account is on the list, press the button
          below on that phone, choose <em>Become a tester</em>, then install from Play.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <a class="cta cta--primary" href={SITE.play.testingUrl} rel="nofollow" data-track="download_click" data-src="beta-primary">
          Open the Play test page →
        </a>
      </p>
      <p class="meta">
        Already a tester? <a href={SITE.play.testingUrl} rel="nofollow">Open the test page directly →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">What to try</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Open one EPUB and one PDF from your own folder.</li>
        <li>Long-press a paragraph, highlight it, and share a quote card.</li>
        <li>Press the audio button and listen with the screen off for a minute.</li>
        <li>Rotate the phone mid-page, then change the font size.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">What helps most</h2>
      <p>
        A sentence about what you expected and what happened — plus the phone model and Android
        version — is worth more than a polished report. Crashes are best sent with the Play
        Console feedback form, or by mail.
      </p>
      <p>
        When testing ends the listing goes public and this page becomes a redirect. Nothing you
        installed is lost.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="meta">
      Not a tester and only want to read? <a href="/reading-craft/">The reading notes are open to
      everyone</a>; <a href="/download/">the download page</a> explains what the app does.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
